From 96760a250e3a2a667f78929290b32418b034374d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:49:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1.21.39: scoped folder exclusions, URI sidecar selection and
 legacy relink (#148 stage C follow-up)

Pure, JVM-tested logic for three items on the migration doc's "Remaining" list, built on the existing
ScopedMediaDiscovery / MediaSource types. Not wired into any production flow; broad access is still
declared and the File scanner is still the Library.

- ScopedMediaDiscovery.scan(excludedFolders): paths relative to the granted root, slash-normalised,
  MediaScanner.scanFolder's rule. Excluded folders are never queried (no provider round trip) and do
  not make the result partial.
- ScopedMediaRecord.sidecars (lyricsUri, artworkUri) chosen from each folder's own listing through a
  per-folder hash index (SidecarIndex), same rules as findMatchingLrc and the thumbnail artwork order.
  A first draft scanned the whole folder per media file (quadratic); the index replaced it and is
  checked against the plain rule. ThumbnailRepository's two constants now come from SidecarNames.
- LegacyDocumentMapping: raw path <-> ExternalStorageProvider document id (longest volume root, '..'
  rejected, cue suffix kept). relinkLegacyMediaIds reports which scoped item a stored id now is, or why
  not (NOT_A_KNOWN_VOLUME_PATH / NOT_IN_SCOPED_LIBRARY / CUE_TRACK_NOT_EXPANDED / UNSUPPORTED_ID); it
  never rewrites stored data and accepts a case-insensitive match only when unique.
  storageVolumeRoots(context) supplies the volume roots.

Verified (standalone Kotlin harness, real sources, real kotlinx-coroutines): the existing 14
ScopedMediaDiscoveryTest cases still pass; 26 new tests pass, including parity with the real
MediaScanner.scanFolder on 40 random trees (excluded folders, hidden look-alikes, Chinese-named
folders under a UTF-8 locale) and fast-index-vs-plain-rule on 400 random folders. Six sabotaged
variants are each caught. Not verified: anything on Android (storageVolumeRoots is only
syntax-checked), no device or real provider, no large-library timing.

Open: reading sidecar bytes, CUE, share/delete (Stage D), exclusions UI, playlist relink wiring.
