+## Stage C follow-up — scoped exclusions, URI sidecar selection, legacy relink (1.21.39 / 262)
+
+Pure, JVM-tested logic for three items from the "Remaining" list below. **None of it is wired into a production flow:** the
+Library is still the File scanner, broad access is still declared, and this change does not reduce the requested permission.
+
+* **Scoped folder exclusions.** `ScopedMediaDiscovery.scan(..., excludedFolders)` takes paths relative to the granted root,
+  slash-normalised, with the same rule as `MediaScanner.scanFolder` (`relative == it || relative.startsWith("$it/")`).
+  An excluded folder is never queried (no provider round trip) and is not reported as a partial result.
+* **URI sidecar selection.** `ScopedMediaRecord.sidecars` (`lyricsUri`, `artworkUri`) is chosen from the names in each
+  folder's own listing with `SidecarIndex`, a per-folder hash index (a folder of thousands of files costs a few lookups per
+  media file, not a scan). Rules are the ones the File flow uses: lyrics `ttml > lrc > srt` by stem, then full media name;
+  artwork same stem, then cover/folder/front/album/artwork. The thumbnail constants are now shared (`SidecarNames`).
+  MediaStore items have no sidecars (it cannot see `.lrc` or cover files). **Reading** the sidecar bytes (ContentResolver
+  streams) and CUE sheets are not implemented.
+* **Legacy path-to-document mapping.** `LegacyDocumentMapping.kt` maps a stored raw path to the ExternalStorageProvider
+  document id and back (`/storage/emulated/0/Music/a.mp3` is `primary:Music/a.mp3`; longest volume root wins; `..` rejected;
+  cue suffix kept). `relinkLegacyMediaIds` answers "which scoped item is this stored id?" for playlists, history, Stack
+  slots and custom order, with a reason when it cannot (`NOT_A_KNOWN_VOLUME_PATH`, `NOT_IN_SCOPED_LIBRARY`,
+  `CUE_TRACK_NOT_EXPANDED`, `UNSUPPORTED_ID`). It never opens a file and never rewrites stored data; a case-insensitive match
+  is accepted only when it is unique. `storageVolumeRoots(context)` supplies the volumes (API 30+ reads `StorageVolume.directory`;
+  below that only the primary volume maps).
+
+### Follow-up verification (standalone Kotlin harness against the real source files)
+
+* The existing 14 `ScopedMediaDiscoveryTest` cases still pass with the modified discovery.
+* 26 new tests pass, including parity with the real `MediaScanner.scanFolder` on 40 random trees (hundreds of media files, excluded
+  folders, hidden look-alikes, Chinese-named folders; run under a UTF-8 locale) and the fast sidecar index against the plain
+  list-scanning rule on 400 random folders. Six deliberately broken variants (prefix-matching exclusion, exclusions never applied,
+  parent path forgotten, wrong lyrics priority, case twins merged, shortest volume root) are each caught.
+* NOT verified: anything on Android. `storageVolumeRoots` was only syntax-checked; no emulator or phone run, no real provider's
+  volume ids, no large-library timing.
+
+### Stage D notes (not started)
+
+* The folder grant persisted today is read-only. Deleting a SAF document needs write access, which is a permission-posture
+  change to decide explicitly; MediaStore items can use the system delete confirmation instead.
+* Sharing a URI item would need a temporary read grant on the intent; exported M3U lists cannot carry Android grants.
+  Both are candidate approaches, unverified.
+
